# Modus Web Components — essentials

For **integration pitfalls** (bootstrap, theme, shell, events, shadow DOM, MCP) on any stack, see [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc). For **`modus-wc-typography`** and text hierarchy, see [modus-typography.mdc](./modus-typography.mdc). For **multi-card pages, card slots, and spacing**, see [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc). For **accessibility** (WCAG 2.1 AA, POUR, semantic HTML, ARIA, testing, inclusive UX), see [modus-accessibility.mdc](./modus-accessibility.mdc). For **Modus CSS variables, spacing scale, radii, and app-level theming next to Modus**, see [modus-setup.mdc](./modus-setup.mdc). For **Angular** (registration, template event bindings, avoiding React-only patterns), see [modus-angular.mdc](./modus-angular.mdc). For **Vue**, see [modus-vue.mdc](./modus-vue.mdc). For **side navigation + navbar hamburger + push/overlay layout**, follow the **modus-wc-side-navigation** Cursor skill **and** the **Side navigation shell — mandatory checklist** below alongside **App shell** in [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc).

## Scaffolding new apps (default shell)

When **creating or scaffolding a new Modus app** (greenfield, starter replacement, or first commit with an empty shell)—unless the user **explicitly** scopes the work to **no side rail** (e.g. embedded widget, single full-bleed surface, marketing page with navbar only):

- **Ship the full standard shell by default:** **`modus-wc-navbar`** (full **`visibility`** on large breakpoints per navbar bullets below) **and** **`modus-wc-side-navigation`** with **responsive** behavior (overlay on narrow, push on wide), **`targetContent`** aimed at the scrolling **`<main>`** column, and **`mainMenuOpen` / `onMainMenuOpenChange`** wired per **modus-wc-side-navigation** Cursor skill: **`overlay`** may **mirror** **`expanded`**; **`push`/desktop `Pattern A`** with an unused **`slot="main-menu"`** should **decouple** **`mainMenuOpen`** (**keep flyout closed**) so empty **`.main-menu`** chrome does **not** sit above **`main`** and swallow clicks (**Navbar — main menu §3.B**).
- **Before coding the shell:** read and apply the **modus-wc-side-navigation** skill (resize/route edge cases, margin sync, z-index, **`mainMenuOpen` mirror vs `push` decouple**, **Pattern A** wrapper width vs **`minWidth`/`maxWidth`**, **`#root` → theme-provider → shell wrappers** flex chain) and the **App shell** + **Viewport height, scroll ownership** sections in [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc); use [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) for the **capped main column** (`max-w-7xl` pattern) and route **Outlet** / single **`<main>`** child.
- **Side nav items:** follow the **Side navigation** bullet under **UX defaults** below (icons in **`start-icon`**, no host padding hacks).
- **Verify in the browser:** When the agent scaffolds a **new** app, **start the dev server** after install and **open IDE browser preview** (or MCP browser) to the local URL the toolchain prints—including an alternate port if the default is taken—unless the user said not to run servers or networking is blocked. Confirms navbar, rail, icons, theme, and scroll ownership without extra back-and-forth.

### Side navigation shell — mandatory checklist (do not skim)

Skipping detail in the **modus-wc-side-navigation** skill commonly ships **main content under an absolute rail** or **overlay mode that still shows a persistent strip**, or **invisible overlays** (**navbar **`.main-menu`** slab** or **`Pattern A`** **fixed** rail wrapper wider than **`minWidth`** on **`push` + collapsed**) that block clicks on **`main`**. **Whenever you implement or change** `modus-wc-side-navigation` with **`targetContent`** and navbar hamburger wiring, **complete all** of the following before considering the shell done:

1. **Read the skill** sections **Overlay mode — full-bleed `targetContent` + collapsed rail shell**, **First paint: push + collapsed**, **First paint: `expanded={true}` on push**, and **Pattern A** (fixed rail / stacking). Do not wire the shell from memory alone.
2. **Single push/overlay breakpoint** — Use **one** exported constant (e.g. `PUSH_LAYOUT_MIN_PX`; **1024** / Tailwind **`lg`** is a common default unless product specifies **768** / **`md`**). Drive from it: **`mode`** (`push` vs `overlay`), **`collapseOnClickOutside`**, and **global CSS** for **`#main-content`** (**`margin-left: 4rem`** or Modus **minWidth** from that width **up** on **`push`**; **`margin-left: 0 !important`** on **`targetContent` for the entire viewport band where `mode === 'overlay'`** — drawer **open and closed** — so **`expanded`** toggles do not jog **`main`**). **The same pixel threshold** must appear in **JS and CSS** (no off-by-one between `767`/`768` and `1023`/`1024` without an explicit rationale).
3. **Push + collapsed** — Never **`marginLeft = ''`** (or equivalent) on **desktop push** when collapsed in a way that strips the **`4rem` / minWidth** reserve; that reproduces **overlap** until or unless **`setTargetContentMargin`** runs. Use the skill’s **stylesheet reserve** + **imperative expanded margin** pattern.
4. **Push + expanded** — In **`useLayoutEffect`**, set **`#main-content`** **`margin-left`** to **`maxWidth` synchronously** before paint, then **double `requestAnimationFrame` re-apply** (Stencil / `setTargetContentMargin` race). See the skill.
5. **Overlay + drawer closed** — The **fixed rail wrapper** must **`width: 0`**, **`overflow: hidden`**, **`pointer-events: none`**. **Do not** set **`aria-hidden="true"`** on that wrapper while focus remains inside the rail (Chrome *Blocked aria-hidden … descendant retained focus* — often **`i.modus-wc-icon`**). Prefer **`inert`** when collapsed and move focus in **`useLayoutEffect`** when **`wrapper.contains(document.activeElement)`** (e.g. to **`#main-content`** or navbar). **`w-0` + `overflow-visible`** is **forbidden** here: Modus’s **collapsed** inner panel can still paint over full-bleed **`main`**. When the drawer **opens** in overlay, restore hit-targets / overflow (and clear **`inert`**) so the panel is usable. **`targetContent`** must stay **full-bleed for the whole overlay band** (not only when closed) — see skill **Overlay mode — full-bleed `targetContent` + collapsed rail shell** and [modus-accessibility.mdc](./modus-accessibility.mdc) → **Collapsed overlay rail shell**.
6. **Mode flips** — When crossing the push/overlay boundary, use a **`key`** on **`modus-wc-side-navigation`** (or equivalent remount) if **`mode`** changes leave stale layout inside the custom element.
7. **Verify** — Resize across the breakpoint, **hard refresh** with push **collapsed** and **expanded**, and exercise **hamburger + overlay** on narrow widths; confirm **no horizontal jog** of **`main`** when toggling the overlay drawer (full-bleed **`targetContent`** on the overlay band). Smoke **pointer:** with **`push`** **collapsed**, click **`main`** well right of the rail—hits must reach in-page controls (****modus-wc-side-navigation** Cursor skill**: wrapper width + **`mainMenuOpen`** **§3**).
8. **Pointer-hit guardrails (**`mainMenuOpen` **+ fixed rail shell)** — Wire **`mainMenuOpen`** per ****modus-wc-side-navigation** Cursor skill Navbar — main menu §3** (**mirror overlay** vs **`push`/desktop decouple when `slot="main-menu"` is unused**). **Fixed** rail wrapper matches **collapsed (**`minWidth`**) vs expanded (**`maxWidth`**)** on **`push`**—see skill integr. checklist **§14–15**.

This checklist is summarized again under **App shell** in [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc).

## Modus-only surface (critical)

These expectations apply whenever the product is **Modus-branded** or **Trimble Modus** is the design system of record.

- **Default to Modus Web Components** for interactive UI, chrome, and data presentation—**not** raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<table>`, or bespoke Tailwind “components” that duplicate what Modus already provides. Reserve plain HTML for **semantic structure** and cases with **no Modus equivalent** after you have checked the catalog (e.g. **Modus Docs MCP** → `_all_components` or the specific tag).
- **Do not combine Modus with shadcn/ui** (or other parallel component libraries built on Radix, MUI, Chakra, etc.). They introduce a second token model, interaction layer, and accessibility contract; the result is inconsistent UX and fragile maintenance. Greenfield and migrations should **standardize on Modus only**; if a starter ships shadcn, **replace** those pieces with Modus—do not interleave both in the same app shell.
- **Favor a correct Modus integration over shipping quickly.** Take the time to confirm **package versions**, **theme / `data-theme`**, **events and `detail` shapes**, **slots**, and **asset paths** (see [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc)). A fast but wrong pattern (wrong event, wrong select model, missing styles) costs more than an extra lookup.

## Packages

- **Do not** install or import **`@trimble-oss/modus-web-components`** (hyphenated npm name) or any other **Modus 1.0** / legacy **`modus-web-components`** npm variant — **deprecated**. Use only **`@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents`** (no hyphen) and the **`@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-*`** framework packages below. *(A static path or folder named `modus-web-components`, e.g. `public/modus-web-components/modus-icons.css`, is unrelated and is fine.)*

Always install **from npm’s current release**: use `@latest` where a single tag is correct, or read **`npm view … version`** / **`versions --json`** so base and framework packages stay on the **same semver** (framework builds append `-react{N}`, `-ng{N}`, or `-vue`).

| Stack | Package(s) | How to resolve the version |
|-------|------------|----------------------------|
| **Vanilla / base only** | `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents` | `npm install @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents@latest --save-exact` |
| **React** | `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react` only (includes base) | If your React major matches the wrapper’s **`latest`** tag: `npm install @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react@latest --save-exact`. Otherwise pick the **newest** dist tag ending in `-react17`, `-react18`, or `-react19` from `npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react versions --json` and install that exact string. |
| **Angular** | `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents` + `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-angular` | Use one base semver for both, e.g. `MVC=$(npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents version)` then `npm install @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents@$MVC @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-angular@${MVC}-ng19 --save-exact` (replace `ng19` with `ng17` / `ng18` / `ng19` to match your Angular major). |
| **Vue** | `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents` + `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-vue` | `MVC=$(npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents version)` then `npm install @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents@$MVC @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-vue@${MVC}-vue --save-exact`. |

- **Angular / Vue:** register per package docs (`defineCustomElements`, `CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA`, etc.).
- Prefer **`--save-exact`** after you’ve chosen the resolved version string.

**Inspect what npm considers current:**

```bash
npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents version
npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react dist-tags
npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react versions --json
npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-angular versions --json
npm view @trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-vue dist-tags
```

## Styles

- Import `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents/modus-wc-styles.css` from the **app entry or first global stylesheet** **before** Tailwind and other application CSS.
- Do not load Modus global styles after your utility or framework CSS in a way that breaks intended cascade.
- When you follow **modus-blueprint’s** stack, **[`src/styles/globals.css`](../../src/styles/globals.css)** layers **app tokens on `:root`** (e.g. **`--padding-card`**, **`--text-xs`…`--text-3xl`**, **`--app-elevation-sm`** / **`--app-elevation-md`**) and documents that **color stays on Modus** (`[data-theme^='modus-modern']` from the package)—**no parallel shadcn-style palette**. An **`@theme inline`** block then **maps Modus variables into Tailwind v4 theme tokens** (`--color-base-page`, **`--color-chart-1`…`--color-chart-5`**, **`--shadow-sm`** / **`--shadow-md`** → elevations, **`--radius-*`** → Modus radii). Keep cascade **Modus package CSS → this `globals.css` → Tailwind / utilities** unless your product documents a different contract.

## Component styling (hosts and overrides)

- **Avoid inline styles** (`style` attributes, React `style={{ … }}`) unless **unavoidable**—e.g. a value that **must** be computed at runtime and **cannot** be modeled with a class plus **CSS custom properties**, or a hard constraint from a third-party embed. Default to **classes**, **Modus tokens** in stylesheets (`var(--modus-wc-…)`), and **utility/layout** classes on the component host.
- **`customClass` is the default** for host-level appearance and layout tweaks on Modus components (margins, width caps, flex, responsive helpers). On React wrappers use the **`customClass`** prop; in other stacks use the documented host/class API for that package. **Order of preference:** documented **props** (`variant`, `size`, `color`, `bordered`, etc.) → **`customClass`** (or equivalent) → **scoped CSS** against predictable hooks → **`::part` / deep selectors** only when the public API cannot reach the surface (confirm with **Modus Docs MCP** for your **`version`**). Do not jump to shadow piercing or global tag hacks when **`customClass`** on the host would suffice.

## Icons

### Font loading (required, not sufficient)

- Serve a small `modus-icons.css` with `@font-face` pointing at **Modus Icons** on jsDelivr; `<link>` it from HTML. Preload woff2 fonts optionally. Full pattern: [modus-wc-icons-setup skill](../skills/modus-wc-icons-setup/SKILL.md).
- Loading the font correctly **does not** prove each `name` is valid—wrong names still render as **blank space** or tofu while other icons on the page look fine.

### Valid `name` values (mandatory when adding or changing icons)

- **`modus-wc-icon` `name` must exist in `@trimble-oss/modus-icons`** for the **`variant`** you use (**outlined** vs **solid**). Do **not** invent, guess, or reuse names from other icon libraries (e.g. generic words like `folder` or `book` may not exist—often the set uses **`folder_closed`**, **`folder_project`**, **`document`**, **`bookings`**, etc.).
- **Source of truth:** icon **`*.svg`** files under **`dist/modus-outlined/svg/`** or **`dist/modus-solid/svg/`** in **`@trimble-oss/modus-icons`** at the **same major** as your jsDelivr pin (see skill). **`name`** on the component = **basename without `.svg`**, with **every hyphen replaced by an underscore** (e.g. `folder-project.svg` → **`folder_project`**).
- **Before merging new or updated icon names:** confirm the file exists for that variant (install dev **`@trimble-oss/modus-icons@…`** and list the folder, open the package **`dist/.../css/index.html`** gallery, use [Modus Icons](https://modus-icons.trimble.com/), or cross-check **`modus-wc-mcp`** / docs). TypeScript types **`name` as `string`**—the compiler will not catch mistakes.
- Match **`variant`** to the set (`outlined` vs `solid`); an icon may exist in one set only.
- No emoji or third-party icon fonts as substitutes.

## Theme

- Before first paint, set on `<html>`: `data-theme` = `modus-modern-light` or `modus-modern-dark`, `data-mode` = `light` | `dark` | `system`, and `class` including `light` or `dark` for the **resolved** mode.
- Keep `localStorage` aligned: `theme` (user choice) and `modus-theme-config` (JSON with `theme` as Modus expects).
- Default new users to **system**; surface the **Modus theme switcher** where the app exposes theme control.

## Custom elements / events

- Prefer **documented custom events**, not raw DOM `click` alone, and do not assume `detail` shape without checking docs.
- **Buttons:** `buttonClick` (React `onButtonClick`, Vue `@button-click`, Angular `(buttonClick)`, vanilla `addEventListener('buttonClick', …)`).
- **Text inputs / select / textarea / number input:** `inputChange`; `detail` is a native `InputEvent`. Read the value from `e.detail?.target?.value` (never `String(e.detail)` — that yields `"[object InputEvent]"`).
- **Select:** options come from the **`options: ISelectOption[]`** prop, NOT slotted `<option>` children (those render as light-DOM orphans next to an empty combobox). Prefer the built-in `label` prop over wrapping in `<label>` + `ModusWcInputLabel`.
- **Checkbox / switch / radio:** `inputChange`; `detail` is also a native **`InputEvent`** (matches text inputs). Read the boolean from **`e.detail?.target?.checked`** — **not** `e.detail` (that is an event), **not** `e.detail.newValue` (legacy 1.0 shape, removed in 2.0). The host's **`value`** prop is **boolean** for these controls, so write back **`Boolean(e.detail?.target?.checked)`**.
- Centralize readers in a small util — `readInputString(e)` for text/select/number/textarea, `readInputChecked(e)` for checkbox/switch/radio. Both read from **`e.detail.target`** (the underlying native `<input>`); only the property differs (`value` vs `checked`). Full pattern and migration table: [**modus-wc-form-inputs**](../skills/modus-wc-form-inputs/SKILL.md).
- Other controls: follow the event names and payloads in Modus docs for that component.

## Framework hooks (minimal)

| Stack | Bootstrap |
|-------|-----------|
| **React** | Wrap the tree with `ModusWcThemeProvider`. If the app is not served from `/`, set `setAssetPath` to the correct origin + public base (e.g. Vite `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`). |
| **Angular** | Call `defineCustomElements()` from the loader; allow custom elements in templates (`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` or equivalent). |
| **Vue** | Follow `@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-vue` setup (registration / plugin as documented). |
| **Vanilla** | Import the bundle or loader so custom elements are defined before first use. |

## Tokens and typography

- Avoid ad-hoc hex for UI chrome: use Modus CSS variables (`--modus-wc-color-base-page`, `base-100`, `base-200`, `base-content`, `base-content-low-contrast`, primary and semantic colors).
- Use `modus-wc-typography` for headings and body with a clear hierarchy; use variables for text color (muted via the low-contrast token). For **`modus-wc-typography`** / **`ModusWcTypography`** props, semantic heading levels, and blueprint alignment, see [modus-typography.mdc](./modus-typography.mdc).
- Use **Open Sans** (e.g. Google Fonts) for body/app text unless the stack already provides it.

## Component selection (Modus-first)

The **Modus-only surface** section above is the gate: stay inside Modus for UI primitives, then apply the selection rules below.

- **Reach for a Modus component before writing custom markup.** For every atomic UI need — badges, chips, avatars, progress bars, toolbars, tables, tabs, tooltips, inputs, modals, switches, cards, alerts, dividers — look up the official component via **Modus Docs MCP** (`get_modus_component_data`, or `_all_components` for the catalog) for your installed **`version`** **before** building it out of `div`s and Tailwind utilities.
- **Common Modus primitives to use instead of hand-rolled equivalents:**
  - Status pills / tags → **`modus-wc-badge`** — defaults and **`color`** usage: **Badges (`modus-wc-badge`)** below. Do **not** style a `<span>` with `rounded-full` + background color.
  - Initials bubbles → **`modus-wc-avatar`** (`initials`, `imgSrc`, `shape`, `size`). Do **not** build a `rounded-full h-8 w-8` div.
  - Progress bars, PTO / quota meters, completion tracks → **`modus-wc-progress`** (or `variant="radial"`). Do **not** stack two background/foreground `div`s with a percentage width.
  - Filter / dense toolbar rows **outside** a single card's body — e.g. **page-level** or **full-width section** headers with search, multiple filters, and grouped actions → **`modus-wc-toolbar`** with `start` / `center` / `end` slots when that density matches the component.
  - **Inside a parent `modus-wc-card`** (card **body**, or a slim row between **`slot="title"`** and main content such as charts/tables): **prefer a `flex` row** (`w-full`, `min-w-0`, `items-center`, and **`justify-between`** only when there are **both** leading and trailing clusters — see [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) **Title row**) composing **`modus-wc-typography`**, **`modus-wc-button`**, selects, etc. **Do not** default to **`modus-wc-toolbar`** here; its chrome is heavy for caption-only or two-cluster rows and reads like a second header. Reserve **`modus-wc-toolbar`** for card-internal use only when the row is **genuinely toolbar-dense** (several controls across slots) and product intent matches that component.
  - **Recharts 3 in cards:** use [.cursor/skills/modus-wc-chart-colors/SKILL.md](../skills/modus-wc-chart-colors/SKILL.md) **§4b** — **`ResponsiveContainer`** needs **positive `initialDimension`**, a **pixel-height** chart wrapper, and charts must not stay mounted under **`hidden`** for inactive full-page views (prevents **`width(-1) height(-1)`** warnings and empty charts).
  - Tabular data → **`modus-wc-table`** with `columns` / `data` and `cellRenderer: (value, row) => string | HTMLElement`. Build a small DOM-cell helper to compose nested Modus WCs (`modus-wc-badge`, `modus-wc-avatar`, `modus-wc-progress`, `modus-wc-chip`, `modus-wc-icon`) inside cells. Do **not** write raw `<table>/<tr>/<th>/<td>` with custom `Th` / `Td` JSX wrappers. Deep patterns: [**modus-wc-table**](../skills/modus-wc-table/SKILL.md).
  - Non-navigational tags / category labels → **`modus-wc-chip`**. **Facet / multi-select filter rows** (toggle, remove, wire to **`modus-wc-table`**): [modus-filters-and-chips.mdc](./modus-filters-and-chips.mdc).
  - Section separators → **`modus-wc-divider`**. Do **not** use `<hr>` or border hacks.
  - Dropdown selections → **`modus-wc-select`** (**`options: ISelectOption[]`** prop, built-in `label`). Do **not** pass slotted `<option>` children.

### Badges (`modus-wc-badge`)

- **Default — neutral, high-contrast filled:** For labels that do **not** convey workflow status or severity (categories, counts, section tags, generic metadata), use **`variant="filled"`** with **neutral / base-contrast** treatment so the badge stays readable on page chrome. Confirm **`variant`**, **`color`**, and defaults with **Modus Docs MCP** for your **`version`**.
- **Semantic `color` only when adding information:** Set **`color`** (e.g. danger, warning, success, primary — confirm allowed values in MCP) **only** when the badge communicates **status, severity, or semantic state** (e.g. Active, Error, Pending, Offline). Do **not** sprinkle semantic colors on decorative or categorical labels where neutral filled suffices.
- **Outlined / subdued:** Use **`variant="outlined"`** for **de-emphasized** tags (optional metadata, dense rows, muted or line-through tone), not as the universal default.
- **Wrapper split:** Prefer **`StatusBadge({ status })`** (maps enum → semantic **`color`**) vs **`TagBadge({ label })`** (neutral filled) so status styling stays centralized and neutral tags do not pick arbitrary **`color`** values.

- **Tailwind fills gaps; it does not replace components.** Tailwind utilities are for **layout, spacing, and composition** (grids, flex, `min-w-0`, `gap-*`, responsive column spans, `max-w-*`, `truncate`, `tabular-nums`). They are **not** for reproducing interactive Modus atoms that already exist — if you catch yourself styling a `<span>` or `<div>` to look like a badge, avatar, chip, progress, or divider, stop and switch to the Modus component.
- **Thin wrappers are fine; re-implementations are not.** A helper like `EligibilityBadge({ status })` that maps a domain enum to `<ModusWcBadge color={...}>{label}</ModusWcBadge>` is useful abstraction (align with **Badges (`modus-wc-badge`)** above for when **`color`** is justified). A helper that returns a hand-styled `<span className="rounded-full ...">` is technical debt — keep the mapper, swap its internals to the Modus component.
- **Composed custom components stay custom only when they are genuinely composite** (KPI tiles, page headers, Gantt canvases, sparkline histograms, and similar multi-element compositions Modus does not ship). When custom is justified, **build from Modus primitives** (`ModusWcCard`, `ModusWcIcon`, `ModusWcTypography`, tokens) + Tailwind layout — not hex colors and `rounded-*` divs.
- **When unsure:** call **`get_modus_component_data`** with **`_all_components`** (for your installed **`version`**) to scan the catalog before hand-rolling anything new.
- **Dialogs:** prefer **`modus-wc-modal`** over bespoke overlays — [**modus-wc-modal**](../skills/modus-wc-modal/SKILL.md).

## UX defaults

- **Component defaults first, then context:** Prefer each control’s **documented defaults** and **standard props** (variant, size, slots, `customClass`) and only change what **layout, density, or use case** needs. Reach for **supported APIs** and **tokens** before ad-hoc CSS or shadow piercing. If the user shares a **detailed Modus-oriented spec** or asks for a **specific customization** within component APIs, adjust props or add **scoped** styling. When the reference is a **screenshot or non-Modus mockup**, follow **Recreating designs from screenshots** (next subsection): **structure and supported styling first**—do not sacrifice maintainability to match unsupported chrome. Still avoid unmaintainable globals or fragile DOM hacks when a **documented** option can achieve the same outcome.

### Recreating designs from screenshots

When implementing a **reference image** or legacy UI with Modus:

- **Build as much as possible from Modus components** — correct tags, slots, hierarchy, density, and **documented configuration** (props, variants, theme). Matching **information architecture and interaction** matters more than cosmetic deltas Modus does not support.
- **Accept styling gaps** that cannot be achieved **out of the box** (public props, tokens, reasonable **`customClass`** on the host). Do not add shadow piercing, global overrides, or inline hacks solely to clone a pixel-level treatment the screenshot shows but Modus does not offer as an API.
- **Ignore non-configurable background and shell fills** from the reference: e.g. **custom-colored** navbar, side navigation rail, or full-page backdrop (**blue, black, brand-tinted**, etc.) when those are **not** a Modus **prop or theme surface**. **Do not** add **decorative SVG / `background-image` patterns on the side-nav rail** (blueprint-style **`Sidenavpattern.svg`**, mesh textures, marketing-only overlays) unless the **product asks for them** — the WC uses **`--modus-wc-color-base-page`** by default and that is sufficient for scaffolding. Keep **Modus default chrome** and **semantic tokens** (`--modus-wc-color-base-*`, theme on `<html>`) so light/dark and upgrades stay valid. Recoloring shell components to “paint-match” a screenshot is an anti-pattern unless the product explicitly requires an approved Modus customization path.
- **Always use Modus dynamic color variables instead of static hex values** — e.g. `--modus-wc-color-base-page`, `--modus-wc-color-base-100`, `--modus-wc-color-base-200`, `--modus-wc-color-base-content`, `--modus-wc-color-base-content-low-contrast`, and semantic tokens (`--modus-wc-color-primary`, error, warning, etc.) so light/dark and theme updates stay correct.
- At most **one primary** (`filled` + primary) control per section or page; default most **low-emphasis** actions to **`color="tertiary"`** with **`variant="outlined"`** or **`borderless`** (see **`modus-wc-button` `color`** next).
- **Primary (`filled` + `primary`) actions should include a leading icon** that matches the action’s meaning (**Export** → **`export`**, **Download** → **`download`**, **Add** / **Create** → a valid **`add`** / **`add_circle`** / domain-specific glyph from **`@trimble-oss/modus-icons`**, etc.). Place **`modus-wc-icon`** **before** the label inside **`modus-wc-button`**; use **`decorative`** when the button text already names the action. **Validate** every **`name`** against the icon package for the chosen **`variant`** (see **Icons** above)—invalid names render as blank space. **Exceptions:** product explicitly forbids icons on that control, or **no suitable glyph** exists in the catalog after checking **Modus Docs MCP** / icon gallery—then ship **text-only** and note why; do **not** guess names from other libraries.
- **`modus-wc-button` `color` — `secondary` is not "the second button."** In Modus, **`secondary`** is a **semantic color role** (often a **warm / gold-adjacent** treatment under **Modus Modern**), **not** a neutral de-emphasis for "any non-primary control." **Do not** use **`color="secondary"`** by default on **`ModusWcButton`** / **`modus-wc-button`** for Cancel, Back, Clear, "Load sample", "Add to canvas", header utility clusters, overflow menus, or other **quiet** actions — use **`color="tertiary"`** with **`outlined`** or **`borderless`**. Reserve **`color="secondary"`** only when **product** or **Modus Docs MCP** explicitly requires the **secondary** brand semantic (distinct from primary), not as a stand-in for "secondary action" in the English sense.
- **Review heuristic:** treat **`color="secondary"`** on **`ModusWcButton`** in a diff as **suspicious** unless justified; prefer **`tertiary`** for de-emphasis. **`ModusWcBadge`**, **`modus-wc-chip`**, and other **non-button** components may still use **`secondary`** when that **status / token** is intentional — this **`secondary` → `tertiary`** default applies to **buttons**.
- **Interactive control size:** Default **`size="sm"`** on **`modus-wc-button`**, **`modus-wc-badge`**, **`modus-wc-chip`**, and similar **compact interactive** components unless **density, touch targets, or documentation** call for **`md`** / **`lg`** (confirm allowed values with **Modus Docs MCP** for your package **`version`**). **Exception:** **`modus-wc-navbar`** slot buttons stay **`size="md"`** per the navbar bullets below.
- **Buttons with icons:** When **`modus-wc-button`** includes **`modus-wc-icon`**, set the icon **one size smaller** than the button (e.g. **`sm`** button + **`xs`** icon, **`md`** button + **`sm`** icon). If the button is already the **smallest** **`size`**, use the **smallest** documented icon **`size`**. Confirm valid **`size`** steps with **Modus Docs MCP**.
- **Icon-only buttons (no visible text label):** When children are **only** **`modus-wc-icon`** (no slotted/visible label text on the button), set **`shape="square"`** on **`modus-wc-button` / `ModusWcButton`** — this is the **documented** configuration for icon-only affordances, not a cosmetic extra. Pair with an accessible name: **`aria-label`** on the **button** (preferred) or **`aria-label`** on the icon with **`decorative={false}`** on **`modus-wc-icon`**. **Audit:** icon-only hosts missing **`shape="square"`** or missing an accessible name.
- Cards: default **`bordered="false"`** and **`padding="compact"`** on **`ModusWcCard`** / **`modus-wc-card`** (set it explicitly on new cards—do not rely on unstated assumptions). Use **`padding="comfortable"`** only when the layout or content needs more inset. Avoid extra decorative borders; gaps between cards, slot usage, title row, body rhythm, and footer alignment: [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc).
- **Tables (`modus-wc-table` / `ModusWcTable`):** Use the **`zebra`** prop for alternating row backgrounds—**do not** recreate zebra striping with **`nth-child`**, row-level background utilities, or ad-hoc CSS when the component already supports it. Confirm the exact prop name and behavior with **Modus Docs MCP** (`modus-wc-table`, your package **`version`**); custom styling is only for gaps MCP cannot cover.
- **Always include a Modus navbar** (`modus-wc-navbar`) at the top of the application as the **preferred** shell. For **new apps**, treat **navbar + side navigation** as the default pair—see **Scaffolding new apps** above.
  - **Typography in navbar slots** (`start`, `center`, `end`): use **`ModusWcTypography`** with **`size="md"`** by default so titles, breadcrumbs, and inline labels match Modus chrome scale (confirm allowed values with **Modus Docs MCP** for your version).
  - **Buttons in navbar slots:** use **`ModusWcButton`** (and other toolbar controls that expose **`size`**) at **`size="md"`** by default—**`xs`** is for **card title rows**, not global navbar chrome (see [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc)).
  - **Built-in navbar controls:** Prefer the **full standard chrome** from **`modus-wc-navbar`** as documented in **Modus Docs MCP** (`get_modus_component_data` → `modus-wc-navbar`, pass your package **`version`**): on desktop-class widths, **`visibility`** should normally include **`mainMenu`**, **`apps`**, **`search`**, **`notifications`**, **`help`**, **`user`**, and **`logo`**, plus **`ai`** and **`searchInput`** when those product features exist—wire the documented events (`mainMenuOpenChange`, `appsClick`, `searchClick`, `notificationsClick`, `helpClick`, `userMenuOpenChange`, `aiClick`, etc.). The component’s **built-in** prop default may hide most items; **apps should override** toward that full set unless requirements explicitly slim the bar. **Narrow viewports:** progressive disclosure (e.g. hamburger + user only) is acceptable; restore the fuller map from **`md`** / **`lg`** up.
  - **`slot="center"` on narrow viewports:** Treat inline titles and dense **`slot="center"`** chrome as **desktop-only** — page **`h1`** in **`main`** carries the title on mobile. Use **one stable** slotted **`div`**, **`hidden={!isWide}`**, **omit Tailwind `flex` / `flex-1` on that node when `hidden`** (author **`display: flex`** breaks **`[hidden]`**), and add **unlayered** **`.app-shell modus-wc-navbar [slot='center'][hidden] { display: none !important; }`** in globals **after** **`@import 'tailwindcss'`** — [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **App shell navbar**; **do not** conditional-mount the center slot ([**modus-wc-react-slotted-hosts**](../skills/modus-wc-react-slotted-hosts/SKILL.md)).
- **Side navigation:** every primary **`modus-wc-menu-item`** in **`modus-wc-side-navigation`** must include a **`modus-wc-icon`** (valid Modus `name`) in **`slot="start-icon"`** so each destination has a consistent glyph in collapsed and expanded states; avoid text-only rail items. **Do not** add horizontal **`padding`** on the **`modus-wc-menu-item` host** for layout—Modus already insets the inner row **button**; host padding **doubles** the left/right gutter.
- Inline editing (**table cells**, **dense grid edit mode**): **`modus-wc-text-input`** / peers **may** use **`bordered="false"`** so the row does not visually double-stack chrome. That exception does **not** apply to standalone forms, dialogs, schedule/calendar pickers, or **`modus-wc-date`** / **`modus-wc-time-input`** unless the design explicitly specifies borderless—see [modus-form-bordered-default.mdc](./modus-form-bordered-default.mdc).
- Host tweaks and overrides: follow **Component styling** — **`customClass`** (or framework equivalent) before shadow piercing or broad globals; see that section for inline-style and `::part` guidance.
- Icons: **one icon per action**; `decorative` when purely visual; otherwise provide an accessible name / `aria-label`.

## React + Modus (slots)

- Skip **`React.StrictMode`** around Modus-heavy trees unless you have verified it: dev **double-mount** plus **named slots** can trigger **`removeChild` / NotFoundError** when slotted nodes reparent.
- **Route views in `<main>`:** Prefer **one** main content column and swap **inner** content (optionally **`key={route}`**) instead of several **sibling** full-page stacks toggled with **`hidden`**—**`gap`** on each stack only applies **inside** that stack, not between route roots, so the next page title can sit **flush** under the previous page’s last card. Use **`Outlet`** / a single layout child with React Router when possible. Full pattern and typography notes: [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc), section **React + slots** → **Route views**.
- Do **not** mount/unmount children that use **`slot="..."`** on a Modus host for UI toggles—keep them in the tree and toggle with **`hidden`** or CSS (`display: none` / class). **Global shell `slot="center"`:** **`[hidden]`** plus **`flex`** / **`hidden md:flex`** on the **same** node **keeps** the row visible — use **conditional `className`** and **unlayered** **`[slot='center'][hidden]`** CSS per [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **App shell navbar**.
- Do **not** swap **entire alternate default-slot bodies** inside the same **`ModusWcCard`** (or other slotted `ModusWc*` host) with a **ternary** (`{a ? <TreeA /> : <TreeB />}`)—Stencil slot **projection** vs React **reconciliation** can leave **orphan** DOM or render the new branch **outside** the card. Use **two stable wrappers** and **`hidden`** / **`aria-hidden`** (see [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc) **Slot projection vs React reconciliation**, [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) **Card slots**, and [**modus-wc-react-slotted-hosts**](../skills/modus-wc-react-slotted-hosts/SKILL.md)). These rules are about **slotted Modus hosts**, not the **page-level** column structure above.

## Cards (defaults)

- **`padding="compact"`** is the **default** for **`modus-wc-card`** in Modus-branded apps: use it unless **`comfortable`** is justified (spacious forms, hero modules, or documented exceptions such as stack-specific notes). Prefer **`comfortable`** over ad-hoc padding hacks when more air is truly needed. Full card composition (title / body / **`slot="footer"`** actions, **`gap-1`** in body, footer inset): [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc).
- **Card-internal rows** (range labels, actions above a chart): prefer **flex + Modus primitives** over **`modus-wc-toolbar`** unless the row is a dense multi-control bar — see **Component selection** above.

## Optional layout CSS

- **`--padding-card: 1rem`** and stacked parent-level card rhythm: see [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) and [modus-setup.mdc](./modus-setup.mdc).

## Ship checklist (Modus UI)

Before merging or handing off Modus-heavy UI, verify:

1. **`package.json`** semver for **`@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents`** matches every **Modus Docs MCP** **`version`** argument (no guessed APIs).
2. **Styles:** **`modus-wc-styles.css`** before Tailwind/app CSS; theme **`data-theme`** / **`data-mode`** / **`light`/`dark`** class on **`<html>`** per **Theme** above.
3. **Surface:** no parallel **shadcn**/Radix/MUI controls in the shell; no raw **`<button>`**, **`<input>`**, **`<select>`**, **`<table>`** where Modus ships **`modus-wc-*`** — spot-check against MCP **`_all_components`** when unsure. **`modus-wc-card`** defaults: **`bordered={false}`**, **`padding="compact"`** unless **`comfortable`** is justified ([modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **Card defaults**).
4. **Forms:** **`inputChange`** / **`detail`** paths match [**modus-wc-form-inputs**](../skills/modus-wc-form-inputs/SKILL.md); **`modus-wc-select`** uses **`options`**, not slotted **`<option>`**. **Field chrome:** keep **`bordered`** default **on** (omit or **`bordered={true}`**) everywhere except the **inline table / grid edit** exception in [modus-form-bordered-default.mdc](./modus-form-bordered-default.mdc)—including on dashboards and in dense toolbars.
5. **Shell scroll:** if **`<main>`** owns vertical scroll, **`min-height: 0`** and **column flex** (**`flex: 1`**) run through **every** link from **`#root` → `#root > modus-wc-theme-provider` → viewport-filling app wrappers** (e.g. `.root-viewport`, `.app-shell`) → the row containing **`main`** — not only the theme provider. **`app-wrapper > modus-wc-theme-provider`** selectors are invalid (wrong DOM order). Full pattern: [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc) → **Viewport height, scroll ownership**.
6. **Page column gutters:** Capped **`main`** / **`max-w-7xl`** wrappers keep **horizontal inset on all breakpoints** — at least **`px-4`** on small / **`narrow`** / container-tight bands; do **not** default to **`px-0`** for “mobile” unless full-bleed is explicitly specified — [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **Main content max width**.
7. **Side navigation:** if **`modus-wc-side-navigation`** + **`targetContent`** ship, complete the **Side navigation shell — mandatory checklist** (above), especially **§7 Verify** (**pointer smoke** on **`main`**) and **§8 **`mainMenuOpen` / rail shell width****.
8. **Icons:** **`modus-icons.css`** linked; **`modus-wc-icon`** **`name`** values validated for variant (**outlined** / **solid**).
9. **Primary CTAs:** each **`filled` + `primary`** button in a section includes a **leading `modus-wc-icon`** whose **`name`** matches the action and is verified in **`@trimble-oss/modus-icons`**, unless product explicitly waives icons or no suitable glyph exists (document the exception).
10. **Accessibility:** meaningful labels; **icon-only** buttons use **`shape="square"`** and **`aria-label`** (or equivalent) on the host; primary interactions keyboard-reachable — [modus-accessibility.mdc](./modus-accessibility.mdc).
11. **App shell navbar (`slot="center"`)** — stable slotted root, **`hidden`** + **no `flex` when hidden**, unlayered **`.app-shell modus-wc-navbar [slot='center'][hidden]`** override after Tailwind import — [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **App shell navbar**.
12. **Production quality gate** (post-implementation, post-vibe): clean **DevTools console** (no errors / warnings / a11y issues), **no inline styles** unless unavoidable, **semantic HTML** with one `<h1>` and proper landmarks, **complete `<head>`** (`lang`, `charset`, `viewport`, page-specific `title` / `description`, OG/Twitter for public surfaces, theme bootstrap before paint), **§6 Modus icon fix pass** ([**modus-wc-icons-setup**](../skills/modus-wc-icons-setup/SKILL.md) + validated **`modus-wc-icon`** **`name`**s / no blank glyphs), build/types/lint green, and Lighthouse a11y ≥ 95 — full checklist in [modus-production-quality.mdc](./modus-production-quality.mdc).

## Troubleshooting

- **Styles wrong or missing:** Modus CSS import order (before Tailwind/globals); `data-theme` / `data-mode` on `html`.
- **Icons missing / blank glyph:** (1) **`modus-icons.css`** linked early, CDN reachable, **`font-src`** allowed if CSP; (2) **`name`** verified against **`@trimble-oss/modus-icons`** for that **`variant`**—invalid names often show as **empty space** next to labels while other icons work. **Production gate:** run **§6** in [modus-production-quality.mdc](./modus-production-quality.mdc) and [**modus-wc-icons-setup**](../skills/modus-wc-icons-setup/SKILL.md).
- **Inputs break at runtime:** `inputChange` and `e.detail?.target?.value` — do not treat `detail` as the string value for text fields.
- **`main` does not scroll (React + `ModusWcThemeProvider`):** document scroll is locked but **`main`’s `overflow: auto` never wins — extend **`min-height: 0`** and **column flex** (**`flex: 1`**) through **each** wrapper between **`#root > modus-wc-theme-provider`** and **`main`** (e.g. `.root-viewport`, `.app-shell`), not only the theme provider. Confirm you are **not** using **`root-viewport > modus-wc-theme-provider`** (selector matches nothing). Cap **`#root`** at **`100dvh`** (**`height` + `max-height` + `overflow: hidden`**) and lock **`html`/`body`** when **`main`** should own scroll. See [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc) (**Viewport height, scroll ownership**).
- **`main` ignores clicks (“invisible overlay”):** (1) **`mainMenuOpen`** mirroring **`expanded`** with empty **`slot="main-menu"`**—navbar **`.main-menu`** slab; **§3.B decouple on `push`/desktop**, see **modus-wc-side-navigation** Cursor skill. (2) **`Pattern A` fixed** rail wrapper always **`maxWidth`** wide while **`push` + collapsed**—transparent column over **`main`**; match wrapper to **`minWidth`/`expanded`**, same skill (**Default positioning** bullet **2**).
- **Card body “duplicates” or new text appears below `ModusWcCard` after a toggle:** Usually a **ternary-swapped** default-slot body inside a slotted host—use **stable wrappers + `hidden`**, not mount/unmount of alternate roots. See [modus-wc-integration.mdc](./modus-wc-integration.mdc) (**Slot projection vs React reconciliation**).
- **`removeChild` / NotFoundError on resize** inside **`modus-wc-navbar`** (often after toggling **`slot="center"`** with **`{condition ? … : null}`**): **Stencil reparents** slotted nodes; **do not mount/unmount** named-slot roots — keep a **stable** host, **`hidden`**, **omit `flex` when `hidden`**, and **unlayered** **`.app-shell modus-wc-navbar [slot='center'][hidden] { display: none !important; }`** — [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **App shell navbar**, [**modus-wc-react-slotted-hosts**](../skills/modus-wc-react-slotted-hosts/SKILL.md).
- **Navbar center title still visible on mobile:** (1) **`flex` / `hidden md:flex`** on the **same** node as **`hidden`**; (2) missing **unlayered** **`display: none !important`** for **`[slot='center'][hidden]`** after **`@import 'tailwindcss'`**; (3) CSS keyed on **`modus-wc-navbar.app-shell-navbar`** on the **host** or **`>`** direct-child — prefer **`.app-shell modus-wc-navbar [slot='center'][hidden]`** — [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **App shell navbar**, [modus-events-and-overrides.mdc](./modus-events-and-overrides.mdc).
- **Main column flush to screen edges on phones:** **Page wrappers** using **`px-0`** / **`narrow ? 'px-0'`** for “mobile layout” — keep **`.app-shell` / `max-w-7xl`** rhythm with **`px-4`** minimum on small bands — [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc) → **Main content max width** (**Mobile / “narrow” layout branches**).

For deeper patterns and examples, see [modus-setup.mdc](./modus-setup.mdc) in this folder. For card-heavy layout, see [modus-layout.mdc](./modus-layout.mdc). For accessibility standards, workflows, and QA, see [modus-accessibility.mdc](./modus-accessibility.mdc).
